# The item lock in the engine: locked items (custom attribute "chaos_locked" != 0, the crafting bench's Lock button,
# salvage.lua) are never sold, taken by id or thrown away.
# - Item::isChaosLocked() / Item::holdsChaosLocked() (locked, or a container with a locked item inside).
# - Player::removeItemOfType (Lua player:removeItem) skips them: NPC selling, quest and NPC turn-ins, every script that
#   removes by item id. player:removeItem(id, count[, subType[, ignoreEquipped[, includeLocked = false]]]).
# - Lua player:getItemCount(id[, subType[, includeLocked = false]]) does not count them (turn-in checks).
# - The NPC trade window's sale list (ProtocolGame::sendSaleItemList) does not offer them; Game::playerSellItem
#   refuses a sale that only locked copies could fill ("Locked items cannot be sold."), before the NPC script runs.
# - Market: Item::hasMarketAttributes() is false for a locked item (no sell offer, no accepting a buy offer with it).
# - Trash holders (trash cans, lava): the tile refuses a locked item, and TrashHolder::addThing never destroys one.
# Apply after 0001-0008: patch -p1 < 0009-locked-items-never-sold.patch (in the server folder, next to src/).
